title: "KhervePDF: A PDF viewer and annotation editor with built-in Git version history"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kerhervé"
    given-names: "Gwilherm"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6449-1828"
    affiliation: "Department of Materials, Imperial College London"
version: "0.67"
date-released: "2026-07-10"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/gkerherve/KhervePDF"
keywords:
  - PDF
  - annotation
  - document management
  - digital signatures
  - version control
abstract: >-
  KhervePDF is an open-source tabbed PDF viewer and annotation editor.
  It provides annotation tools (pen, highlight, text, shapes, sticky
  notes, signatures, redaction), page operations (insert, delete, rotate,
  reorder, merge, split), AcroForm form filling, full-text search, and
  per-document Git version history with auto-commit and remote push.
  Built with Python, PySide6, PyMuPDF, pikepdf and pygit2.
